# BigYellow Beacon POC — read before any task

## Source of truth (in this order)
1. `docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md`: Kundan's POC design (architecture, features, data model, APIs, AI, sync, security, demo). Section numbers below (§) refer to it.
2. `docs/DECISIONS.md`: defaults where the design is silent or inconsistent. Overrides older material.
3. `contract/beacon_contract/`: the **frozen v1.0 payload contract** (Pydantic). Every request/response body and every sync payload must be one of these models. Do **not** redefine payload shapes elsewhere; import them. Don't edit `contract/` unless the task explicitly says so.
4. `docs/PLAN.md`: hackathon plan, scope tiers P0/P1/P2, owners, milestones.

Anything in older files (`contracts/`, old READMEs, earlier rules) that disagrees with these is obsolete.

## Product in one paragraph
Beacon is an offline-first AI copilot for seafarers' safety and wellbeing, built for the **Google Cloud AI Builder Cup 2026**. On the ship, crew and Master use **one React PWA** served by an **edge server** over the ship LAN (HTTPS via mkcert). Crew report near-misses by voice/photo/text in any language; **Gemma** (Ollama) on the edge structures and translates them; the Master gets an **SSE alert** within a second and acts on board. A transactional outbox syncs **kilobyte deltas** to **shore-api on Cloud Run** when the (simulated) VSAT link is up. Shore reviewers use the **Beacon Dashboard**: **Gemini on Vertex AI** analyses each ticket (similar tickets across the fleet + accident-corpus match), reviewers Accept/Reject, reply anonymously, and publish **microlearnings** back to one, some or all vessels.

## Users (§5)
| Role | App | Login |
|---|---|---|
| `crew` | Crew app, crew view | QR pairing + 4-digit PIN |
| `master` (incl. Safety Officer) | Crew app, Master view | QR pairing + 6-digit PIN (first Master: `make pair-master`) |
| `shore_reviewer`, `shore_admin` | Beacon Dashboard | email + password (JWT) |
| `vessel` (edge device) | shore sync routes | vessel API key + HMAC signature |

There is **no native mobile app** and **no psychologist/escalation role**.

## Non-negotiable rules
1. **Ship works offline.** Nothing on the edge or in the crew app may need the internet at runtime: no CDNs, remote fonts or cloud calls. Models are pulled before the voyage.
2. **Identity never leaves the ship.** Names, crew IDs, device IDs, PINs, audio and transcripts stay on the edge. Shore gets a per-ticket `reporter_ref` (`beacon_contract.security.reporter_ref`), rank band (collapsed to `crew` when < 5 on the vessel), vessel. `SyncDelta` validation rejects forbidden keys; never bypass it.
3. **Scrub before push.** Every free-text field goes through `beacon_contract.privacy.scrub_text(text, roster_names)` before it is written to the outbox. Strip photo EXIF on upload.
4. **Check-in transcripts are never written** to disk, DB or logs. Only scores. Individual scores stay on the edge and are visible only to that crew member.
5. **k ≥ 5** for any wellbeing number shown to the Master or sent to shore (`beacon_contract.privacy.K_ANON`).
6. **Safety rails** run before and after every model call on crew text. On a hit: no model call (or discard output), show the fixed placeholder message, offer "Would you like the Master to check on you?". Welfare alert to the Master = name + time only. Nothing to shore. Rail hits are counted on the edge only.
7. **Never log** report text, check-in text or request bodies. Log IDs, routes, status, latency, rule IDs.
8. **AI suggests, humans decide.** Every model output is validated against a contract model (1 retry with the validation error, then fallback). AI-generated content is labelled with model + time. Nothing auto-applies to a ticket's official fields without a human click.
9. **Field ownership in sync.** Edge owns `onboard_status` and report fields; shore owns `shore_status`, `reject_*`, `assigned_to`. Each side sends only what it owns.

